GT patch 0021: make lcs-recomp's Vulkan GE backend draw GT (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-gpu-ge-backend-design.md,
phase 2; measured with tools/gpu_gate.sh).

- Blending: every GE equation and factor, the way ge_renderer.cpp blend_pixel does (all four channels
  with the same factors); min(1, 2As) / min(1, 2(1-As)) computed in the shader with dual-source blending.
- Targets: every render target covers a fixed 512x512 guest-pixel space at the internal-resolution
  scale (it used to re-map to each draw's stride/scissor, which broke GT's render-to-texture HUD layer
  0x0CC000); the display shows its logical crop; sampling a target as a texture scales the UVs to the
  texture's size.
- Framebuffer formats: the shader blends the unquantized colour and alpha (it used to quantize before
  blending, so a 5551 target blended with a 1-bit alpha); reading a target back as a texture emulates
  the 16-bit pack/unpack the PSP (and ge_renderer.cpp) store.
- Depth: one depth image shared by every target (the PSP has one zbp), never cleared behind the game's
  back; draws that write depth without testing it test ALWAYS (Vulkan never writes depth with its test
  off, so GT's clear-mode depth clears were lost and its cars failed the depth test).
- Textures: keyed by content once their signature is known, and re-checked after a block transfer
  writes their bytes (GT copies every text glyph into the same small texture right before drawing it).
- Present: MAILBOX when the driver has it, also with VSync (FIFO blocked the GE thread ~28 ms per present
  and GT ran at 30 vblank waits/s instead of 120).
- Present under FIFO (the only mode Vulkan guarantees): the acquire never waits; with no free image the
  frame is skipped, so the GE thread never blocks on the monitor.
- InternalResolutionMode=Window (gt_play's default): the smallest whole scale of 480x272 that covers the
  window, capped by MaxInternalScale, followed live on resize/fullscreen (targets rebuilt between frames).
- CPU cost: no rasterizer worker threads by default (they spun idle: 2.4x the CPU for the same speed);
  guest writes stamp 64 KiB pages instead of walking every cached texture; uploaded textures drop their
  CPU copy. Each GPU image carries the vblank it was closed at (the GPU gate pairs by it).
- GT_GPU_STATS also counts draws per target and textures read from VRAM. Vulkan app name "GTNative".
